loorplanning is the first step in the physical design process that establishes the physical layout of the design. Floorplanning involves specifying the core and die size, determining the distance between the core and the I/O boundaries, creating the rows of standard cells, assigning I/O pins, and placing the macros and placement blocks wherever necessary. Properly planned floorplanning allows adequate physical space for the placement of standard cells, as well as for signal and clock routing and power delivery with little congestion and IR drop problems.
